<title>UK: UK govt &quot;has very clear policy&quot; on EMU.</title>
<headline>UK govt &quot;has very clear policy&quot; on EMU.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The opposition Labour party's decision to call for a referendum if, once in power, it decides to join a single currency has had no effect on government policy on Economic and Monetary Union, an aide said on Monday.</p>
<p>The aide from Prime Minister John Major's office said: &quot;The government has a very clear policy which we have spelled out on many occasions.&quot;</p>
<p>Major has already pledged to hold a referendum if a Conservative government decides to take Britain into a single currency. He has said the decision will be taken at the time on the basis of the national interest. -- London newsroom +44 171 542 7768</p>
</text>
